## Cross-project knowledge

Before researching, designing, or implementing a non-trivial change, call the
`search_knowledge` MCP tool with the user's goal, relevant error text, and/or
feature name. Treat retrieved records as leads: inspect the cited repository,
path, and Git revision before relying on them.

After completing work that is likely useful in another project, call
`record_knowledge`. Always include `purpose`, `background`, and `rationale`;
include only non-secret paths and short excerpts. Do not record credentials,
private keys, `.env` values, or personal data.

